Package: superv
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0
Recommends: libxtst6
Description: Clipboard for Linux
 SuperV brings the Windows clipboard history panel (Win+V) to Linux.
 Press Super+V to see the last 25 things you copied (text and images),
 pick one to paste it into the app you are using, pin favourites, and
 clear the rest. Works on GNOME, Cinnamon, MATE and Xfce, on Wayland and
 X11. Never connects to the internet.
